  "description": "Word-level contexts of the two quadratic steps in the Bokut-Shiao corner's a <= b regime. Both apply the SAME rule, heckeRelation j1, and both are preceded by yangBaxterRelation j1 (j1+1). The two contexts differ by one letter at each end: the second occurrence has sigma_{i-2} prepended on the left and lacks the trailing sigma_i on the right. So one general step lemma with arbitrary contexts covers both -- the analogue of monicStep for the three-word quadratic rule.",
  "parameters": {
    "quad_rule": "heckeRelation j1,  j1 = i - a, both occurrences",
    "preceding_rule": "yangBaxterRelation j1 (j1+1), both occurrences",
    "left_context_first": "rel: [1..a-2] ++ [0..a-3] ++ [a-1, a-2, a, a-1]; abs: descWord (i-1) (j1+2) ++ descWord i (j1+3) ++ [s_{j1+1}, s_{j1+2}, s_{j1}, s_{j1+1}]",
    "left_context_second": "[s_{i-2}] ++ left_context_first",
    "right_context_first": "descWord (j1-1) j2 ++ [s_i]",
    "right_context_second": "descWord (j1-1) j2"
  },
